ir and B1, waits on B1 or B5, but loses Prevalent Wind potential.  \n\nSo Play B1 seems best.  \n\nCheck if discarding B1 might be dangerous? B1 is terminal, but previous player has B1 pung, so they might not need it. Others might be waiting for it? Unclear.  \n\nThus, final choice: Play B1.  \n\nReason: Discarding B1 puts you in tenpai with a two-way wait for B5 or F1, maximizing chances to win. Keeping F1 pair offers higher scoring potential via Prevalent Wind and Pung of Terminals or Honors, and if you self-draw F1, you can reach 8 points with combined patterns. Discarding B5 or F1 reduces point potential or leaves less likely waits.  \n\nAnswer: Play B1"}
